# git-LFS for the objects that make this repository heavy.
#
# Measured at the split (2026-10-23): studies/ tracked 151 PNGs (51 MB) and 229 JSONs
# (34 MB), with ~257 MB of packed history. Attributes apply to objects added or modified
# after this file lands; history is NOT rewritten (git lfs migrate would break the
# byte-identical tree-manifest check of the extraction, docs/repo-split-plan.md Step 2).
#
# Small CSV / JSON stay in plain git on purpose: their diffs are a review signal
# (posthoc-reporting), and LFS objects show no diff in a PR.

# Rendered figures: every report embeds them, none is diffed by eye.
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.svg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.npz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Result JSONs above ~1.5 MB (frozen per-trial / per-subject tables, study 09).
studies/09-gru-cross-species-transfer/analysis/matched_half_results.json filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
studies/09-gru-cross-species-transfer/analysis/example_behavior_sessions.json filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
studies/09-gru-cross-species-transfer/analysis/embedding_dimension_results.json filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
studies/09-gru-cross-species-transfer/analysis/embedding_dimension_expansion_results.json filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
